#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8866d4a7-b007-5b5c-8db0-e149a146f1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8866d4a7-b007-5b5c-8db0-e149a146f1d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293463} :answer-field/id #uuid "08e66c54-d1b0-5a37-9793-f7b1b263205c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293954}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c287975d-2210-588b-808c-37d4aa02c574" :question/math-academy-id "q-278395" :question/problem "![](images/33/33adaa159f0926038c6b04a750b6a61b8a18e0fe2df9c6c3c581c139e27b2c95.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(6,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087833 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "57e19ee3-db9a-58d7-8ca3-4e8801aee656" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea709181-3435-5cda-a381-1ffb34dc4957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293847}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea709181-3435-5cda-a381-1ffb34dc4957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293847} :answer-field/id #uuid "b39106f6-0d4a-50b5-a684-3a9dd19496c6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58d53b95-48c4-5460-b91e-ffee8730045f" :question/math-academy-id "q-278398" :question/problem "![](images/44/441ee336bc10f5787a5956a6c118cde9faaa0485c3c2f8a6adb9dd93903b3972.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,5),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d35968d-5c44-5e65-a197-520a366d9bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d35968d-5c44-5e65-a197-520a366d9bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442279} :answer-field/id #uuid "344c48c4-4333-53a2-91c2-910da2275099" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442281} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6350dda7-0009-5d3a-9b8a-8e8d61699c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6350dda7-0009-5d3a-9b8a-8e8d61699c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442280} :answer-field/id #uuid "72c3b159-addc-58ed-8523-aec1a6a17d47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35dee2e4-b90f-575e-8987-9a600b4e60ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-278400" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=2$ and $k=-1,$ so the center is located at $(2,-1).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=18$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=18,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=3\\sqrt{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}=6\\sqrt{2},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295010 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a81632cc-b5b8-5293-854a-15d0e07860c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a81632cc-b5b8-5293-854a-15d0e07860c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293597} :answer-field/id #uuid "17f02c76-60a4-5afe-a558-bf595f597fe6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294003} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fee5cb0e-afb7-5315-bc6f-231125cf2b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fee5cb0e-afb7-5315-bc6f-231125cf2b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293929} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c691bd-bcc5-5404-b7f6-e6dcdb4b61e1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f193e9d2-f5fe-5d88-ae37-9891fd4ddd44" :question/math-academy-id "q-278403" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{15}+\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{49}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=1$ and $k=6,$ so the center is located at $(1,6).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=15$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=15,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{15}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{15}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{15}=2\\sqrt{15}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087834 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5028940-be34-56b7-8947-6129252f06a7" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Center and Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10a7b612-819f-5a1c-a8b0-8ec256d1a50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10a7b612-819f-5a1c-a8b0-8ec256d1a50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293006} :answer-field/id #uuid "6104b68e-20e5-53b0-9017-463931726fac" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294275} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e075ac1-0b6f-5a1b-9f7a-153a820b245a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e075ac1-0b6f-5a1b-9f7a-153a820b245a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293313} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0814c7b-ca42-54f0-a23e-73619c3fcf74" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a4cc48c-e200-5367-abd6-f0488138a7ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-278404" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y+8)^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=3$ and $k=-8,$ so the center is located at $(3,-8).$\n\nIn the given equation, we also have ${a}^{2}=8$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=8,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2}.$"}]}
